                <div class="callout">

                    <div class="callout-title">
                        Digital Input
                    </div>

                    <p>
                        Instead of pushing electricity
                        <strong>out</strong> (Output), the ESP32
                        can listen to a pin to see if electricity
                        is coming <strong>in</strong> (Input).
                    </p>

                </div>

                <p>
                    Because it is "Digital", it only understands
                    two answers:
                </p>

                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>HIGH:</strong>
                        "I detect voltage!"
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <strong>LOW:</strong>
                        "I detect nothing (0 volts)!"
                    </li>
                </ul>


                <div class="callout">

                    <div class="callout-title">
                        The Magic of INPUT_PULLUP
                    </div>

                    <p>
                        If a pin is just floating in the air,
                        the ESP32 gets confused. It might randomly
                        read HIGH or LOW just from the static
                        electricity in your room.
                        <br><br>

                        To fix this, the ESP32 has tiny,
                        invisible resistors built
                        <strong>inside the chip</strong>.
                        By using a mode called
                        <code>INPUT_PULLUP</code>, we turn on
                        a tiny stream of internal power to the pin.
                        <br><br>

                        When the button is
                        <strong>NOT pressed</strong>,
                        the pin feels its own power and reads
                        <strong>HIGH</strong>.
                        <br><br>

                        When you <strong>PRESS</strong> the button,
                        the power is pulled down to Ground,
                        and the pin reads <strong>LOW</strong>.
                    </p>

                </div>


                <div class="callout">

                    <div class="callout-title">
                        Decision Making — if / else
                    </div>

                    <p>
                        We are going to give the ESP32 a brain today.
                        We will tell it:
                        <br><br>

                        <strong>
                            "IF the button is pressed, do this.
                            ELSE (otherwise), do that."
                        </strong>
                    </p>

